Out of memory, Vim's swap file came back with wrong lines: "E317: Pointer block
id wrong", then lines lost or a wrong file written.  Amix's UFS, stock 2.1c as
well, mishandles a 4 Kbyte write to the second half of an 8 Kbyte block: it sets
up the page of the block's first half instead, without reading it, so that page
can hold old memory, not the file's data.  The disk stays right.  Pages of a
whole 8 Kbyte block never write to a block's second half on their own, so the
swap file's pages are now 8 Kbyte on Amix.

--- a/src/memfile.c
+++ b/src/memfile.c
@@ -61,7 +61,14 @@
 # endif
 #endif
 
-#define MEMFILE_PAGE_SIZE 4096		// default page size
+#ifdef __amix__
+// Amix's UFS (stock 2.1c as well) mishandles a 4 Kbyte write to the second
+// half of an 8 Kbyte block: the cached first half can then hold old memory.
+// The swap file rewrites single pages, so give it whole 8 Kbyte blocks.
+# define MEMFILE_PAGE_SIZE 8192
+#else
+# define MEMFILE_PAGE_SIZE 4096		// default page size
+#endif
 
 static long_u	total_mem_used = 0;	// total memory used for memfiles
 
